# Intentionally rule-free. Do not add a catch-all here.
#
# This site is PRE-RENDERED: scripts/prerender.mjs writes a real index.html for
# all twelve addresses, and Cloudflare Pages serves those files directly. An
# unmatched path already returns a correct HTTP 404 without any rule in this
# file (verified against the live host 2026-09-09).
#
# The rule that used to live here was `/*  /index.html  200`, the splat a plain
# single-page app needs. It was doing nothing, because static files take
# precedence over it. On a pre-rendered site a splat targeting a .html file can
# also 308-loop forever, because Pages' own extension-strip redirect re-matches
# it. Leave this file empty of rules.
